 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greetings and goodbyes",
     "texto": [
      "**Здравствуйте** is the formal greeting and works at any time of day. Among friends, you say **привет**.",
      "Depending on the time of day: **доброе утро** (good morning, before noon), **добрый день** (good day, good afternoon) and **добрый вечер** (good evening, good night).",
      "To say goodbye: **до свидания** (goodbye) and, among friends, **пока**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Informal and formal «you»",
     "texto": [
      "**Ты** is «you» (informal) and is usually used with friends, family and children. **Вы** can mean «you» (formal) or «you» (plural). With an adult you do not know, **вы** is a safe choice to start with; the relationship, the setting and the person's preference also matter."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying your name",
     "texto": [
      "In Russian you say «to me they call»: **Меня зовут Анна** = my name is Anna.",
      "To ask it: **Как вас зовут?** (formal) or **Как тебя зовут?** (informal).",
      "You can also just say **Я Антон** (I am Anton): remember that the verb «to be» is not said.",
      "When you meet someone: **очень приятно** («very pleasant»), which is like English «nice to meet you».",
      "**А** is used to turn the question back: **А вы?** (and you? formal), **А ты?** (and you? informal)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
